-- Tests for body-a: Penal Code 1871 Chapter 16, ss 299-358
-- (pc-body-a-life.l4, pc-body-a-hurt.l4, pc-body-a-force.l4).
--
-- Expected values come FROM THE SOURCE: each Illustration is cited on the line
-- above its assertion (`-- s 350 illus (a)`); boundary cases for every age,
-- duration and count are on the helpers, both sides of the line. A failing
-- assertion here is a finding, not a typo: never edit an expected value to
-- make it pass.
--
-- Fixtures are full record literals, every field spelled; a leaf the facts
-- do not make TRUE is FALSE, as the charge generator's schema completion would
-- make it. (They were expanded from a compact spec by a script that checks
-- every field name against the DECLAREs, so a misspelt leaf cannot silently
-- default.)

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `pc-domain`
IMPORT `pc-general`
IMPORT `pc-body-a-hurt`
IMPORT `pc-body-a-force`
IMPORT `pc-body-a-life`

§ `body-a tests`

`the particulars` MEANS Particulars WITH
    accused            IS "A"
    date               IS "the 1st day of January 2026"
    time               IS ""
    place              IS "Orchard Road"
    `co-accused`       IS ""
    `common intention` IS FALSE

§§ `The threshold helpers - both sides of each line`

-- s 320(h): "during the space of 20 days"
#ASSERT `lasts the space of 20 days` 20
#ASSERT NOT `lasts the space of 20 days` 19
-- ss 354(2), 354A(2)(b): "below 14 years of age"
#ASSERT `below 14 years of age` 13
#ASSERT NOT `below 14 years of age` 14
-- s 300 Exception 5: "above 18 years of age" (completed years; F-10)
#ASSERT `above 18 years of age` 18
#ASSERT NOT `above 18 years of age` 17
-- s 300 Exception 6: "below 12 months of age"
#ASSERT `below 12 months of age` 11
#ASSERT NOT `below 12 months of age` 12
-- s 305(2): "minor" - "below 18 years of age"
#ASSERT `below 18 years of age` 17
#ASSERT NOT `below 18 years of age` 18
-- s 312: "more than 16 weeks' duration"
#ASSERT `more than 16 weeks' duration` 17
#ASSERT NOT `more than 16 weeks' duration` 16
-- s 317: "below 12 years of age"
#ASSERT `below 12 years of age` 11
#ASSERT NOT `below 12 years of age` 12

§§ `Hurt - ss 319-335`

-- s 319 Explanation: causing another to be unconscious is causing hurt.
`A knocks Z unconscious` MEANS `Hurt Facts` WITH
    particulars                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              IS `the particulars`
    victim                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   IS "Z"
    `victim described as`                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    IS ""
    `the manner`                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                             IS "by striking the said Z on the head with his fist"
    `caused bodily pain`                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                     IS FALSE
    `caused disease`                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                         IS FALSE
    `caused infirmity`                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                       IS FALSE
    `caused the victim to be unconscious`                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    IS TRUE
    `intention of causing hurt`                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              IS TRUE
    `knowledge of being likely to cause hurt`                                                                                                                                                                                                                                IS FALSE
    `the hurt caused is emasculation`                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        IS FALSE
    `the hurt caused is death`                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               IS FALSE
    `the hurt caused is permanent privation of the sight of either eye`                                                                                                                                                                                                      IS FALSE
    `the hurt caused is permanent privation of the hearing of either ear`                                                                                                                                                                                                    IS FALSE
    `the hurt caused is privation of any member or joint`                                                                                                                                                                                                                    IS FALSE
    `the hurt caused is destruction or permanent impairing of the powers of any member or joint`                                                                                                                                                                             IS FALSE
    `the hurt caused is permanent disfiguration of the head or face`                                                                                                                                                                                                         IS FALSE
    `the hurt caused is fracture or dislocation of a bone`                                                                                                                                                                                                                   IS FALSE
    `the hurt caused endangers life`                                                                                                                                                                                                                                         IS FALSE
    `the hurt caused the sufferer to be in severe bodily pain during the space of 20 days`                                                                                                                                                                                   IS FALSE
    `the hurt caused the sufferer to be unable to follow his ordinary pursuits during the space of 20 days`                                                                                                                                                                  IS FALSE
    `the hurt caused is penetration of the vagina or anus without consent which causes severe bodily pain`                                                                                                                                                                   IS FALSE
    `the hurt which he intends to cause or knows himself to be likely to cause is grievous hurt`                                                                                                                                                                             IS FALSE
    `the hurt which he intends to cause or knows himself to be likely to cause is not grievous`                                                                                                                                                                              IS FALSE
    `by means of any instrument for shooting, stabbing or cutting`                                                                                                                                                                                                           IS FALSE
    `by means of any instrument which, used as a weapon of offence, is likely to cause death`                                                                                                                                                                                IS FALSE
    `by means of fire or any heated substance`                                                                                                                                                                                                                               IS FALSE
    `by means of any poison or any corrosive substance`                                                                                                                                                                                                                      IS FALSE
    `by means of any explosive substance`                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    IS FALSE
    `by means of any substance which it is harmful to the human body to inhale, to swallow, or to receive into the blood`                                                                                                                                                    IS FALSE
    `by means of any animal`                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                 IS FALSE
    `for the purpose of extorting from the sufferer, or from any person interested in the sufferer, any property or valuable security`                                                                                                                                       IS FALSE
    `for the purpose of constraining the sufferer, or any person interested in the sufferer, to do anything which is illegal or which may facilitate the commission of an offence`                                                                                           IS FALSE
    `for the purpose of extorting from the sufferer, or from any person interested in the sufferer, any confession or any information which may lead to the detection of an offence or misconduct`                                                                           IS FALSE
    `for the purpose of constraining the sufferer, or any person interested in the sufferer, to restore any property or valuable security, or to satisfy any claim or demand, or to give information which may lead to the restoration of any property or valuable security` IS FALSE
    `administers to, or causes to be taken by, any person any poison or any stupefying or intoxicating substance, or any substance which is harmful to the human body to inhale, swallow or receive into the blood`                                                          IS FALSE
    `with intent to commit or to facilitate the commission of an offence`                                                                                                                                                                                                    IS FALSE
    `the sufferer is a public servant`                                                                                                                                                                                                                                       IS FALSE
    `in the discharge of his duty as such public servant`                                                                                                                                                                                                                    IS FALSE
    `with intent to prevent or deter that person or any other public servant from discharging his duty as such public servant`                                                                                                                                               IS FALSE
    `in consequence of anything done or attempted to be done by that person in the lawful discharge of his duty as such public servant`                                                                                                                                      IS FALSE
    `on grave and sudden provocation`                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        IS FALSE
    `neither intends nor knows himself to be likely to cause hurt to any person other than the person who gave the provocation`                                                                                                                                              IS FALSE
    `neither intends nor knows himself to be likely to cause grievous hurt to any person other than the person who gave the provocation`                                                                                                                                     IS FALSE
    `the provocation is not sought or voluntarily provoked by the offender as an excuse for doing harm to any person`                                                                                                                                                        IS FALSE
    `the offender did not know and had no reason to believe that the provocation was given by anything done in obedience to the law, or by a public servant in the lawful exercise of his powers`                                                                            IS FALSE
    `the provocation is not given by anything done in the lawful exercise of the right of private defence`                                                                                                                                                                   IS FALSE
#ASSERT `causes hurt` `A knocks Z unconscious`
#ASSERT `voluntarily causes hurt` `A knocks Z unconscious`
#ASSERT `offence under s 323` `A knocks Z unconscious`
#ASSERT NOT (`grievous hurt within section 320` `A knocks Z unconscious`)
#ASSERT (`charge under s 323` `A knocks Z unconscious`)'s text EQUALS "You, A, are charged that you, on or about the 1st day of January 2026, at Orchard Road, Singapore, did voluntarily cause hurt to one Z, to wit, by striking the said Z on the head with his fist, and you have thereby committed an offence punishable under section 323 of the Penal Code 1871."
#ASSERT (`charge under s 323` `A knocks Z unconscious`)'s punishment EQUALS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 3 years, or with fine which may extend to $5,000, or with both"

-- A refusal: the blow causes nothing. s 321 needs hurt in fact.
