    `the sufferer is a public servant`                                                                                                                                                                                                                                       IS FALSE
    `in the discharge of his duty as such public servant`                                                                                                                                                                                                                    IS FALSE
    `with intent to prevent or deter that person or any other public servant from discharging his duty as such public servant`                                                                                                                                               IS FALSE
    `in consequence of anything done or attempted to be done by that person in the lawful discharge of his duty as such public servant`                                                                                                                                      IS FALSE
    `on grave and sudden provocation`                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        IS TRUE
    `neither intends nor knows himself to be likely to cause hurt to any person other than the person who gave the provocation`                                                                                                                                              IS FALSE
    `neither intends nor knows himself to be likely to cause grievous hurt to any person other than the person who gave the provocation`                                                                                                                                     IS TRUE
    `the provocation is not sought or voluntarily provoked by the offender as an excuse for doing harm to any person`                                                                                                                                                        IS TRUE
    `the offender did not know and had no reason to believe that the provocation was given by anything done in obedience to the law, or by a public servant in the lawful exercise of his powers`                                                                            IS TRUE
    `the provocation is not given by anything done in the lawful exercise of the right of private defence`                                                                                                                                                                   IS TRUE
#ASSERT `offence under s 335` `A breaks Z's arm on provocation`
#ASSERT NOT (`offence under s 325` `A breaks Z's arm on provocation`)

§§ `Rash and negligent acts - ss 304A, 335B-338`

`A drives rashly and injures Z` MEANS `Rash Act Facts` WITH
    particulars                                                     IS `the particulars`
    victim                                                          IS "Z"
    `victim described as`                                           IS ""
    `the manner`                                                    IS "by driving motor car SBA1234A through a red light at the junction of Orchard Road and Scotts Road and colliding with the said Z"
    `does the act rashly`                                           IS TRUE
    `does the act negligently`                                      IS FALSE
    `so as to endanger human life or the personal safety of others` IS TRUE
    `knowing or believing that such act is likely to cause death`   IS FALSE
    `causes hurt to any person`                                     IS TRUE
    `causes grievous hurt to any person`                            IS FALSE
    `causes the death of any person`                                IS FALSE
    `not amounting to culpable homicide`                            IS FALSE
#ASSERT `offence under s 337(a)` `A drives rashly and injures Z`
-- s 26F(2): a rash act also makes out the negligent limb.
#ASSERT `offence under s 337(b)` `A drives rashly and injures Z`
#ASSERT `offence under s 336(a)` `A drives rashly and injures Z`
#ASSERT NOT (`offence under s 338(a)` `A drives rashly and injures Z`)
#ASSERT (`charge under s 337(a)` `A drives rashly and injures Z`)'s text EQUALS "You, A, are charged that you, on or about the 1st day of January 2026, at Orchard Road, Singapore, did cause hurt to one Z by doing an act so rashly as to endanger human life or the personal safety of others, to wit, by driving motor car SBA1234A through a red light at the junction of Orchard Road and Scotts Road and colliding with the said Z, and you have thereby committed an offence punishable under section 337(a) of the Penal Code 1871."

`A drives negligently and kills Z` MEANS `Rash Act Facts` WITH
    particulars                                                     IS `the particulars`
    victim                                                          IS "Z"
    `victim described as`                                           IS ""
    `the manner`                                                    IS "by failing to keep a proper lookout while reversing lorry YM1234B and colliding with the said Z"
    `does the act rashly`                                           IS FALSE
    `does the act negligently`                                      IS TRUE
    `so as to endanger human life or the personal safety of others` IS TRUE
    `knowing or believing that such act is likely to cause death`   IS FALSE
    `causes hurt to any person`                                     IS FALSE
    `causes grievous hurt to any person`                            IS FALSE
    `causes the death of any person`                                IS TRUE
    `not amounting to culpable homicide`                            IS TRUE
#ASSERT `offence under s 304A(b)` `A drives negligently and kills Z`
#ASSERT NOT (`offence under s 304A(a)` `A drives negligently and kills Z`)
#ASSERT (`charge under s 304A(b)` `A drives negligently and kills Z`)'s text EQUALS "You, A, are charged that you, on or about the 1st day of January 2026, at Orchard Road, Singapore, did cause the death of one Z by doing a negligent act not amounting to culpable homicide, to wit, by failing to keep a proper lookout while reversing lorry YM1234B and colliding with the said Z, and you have thereby committed an offence punishable under section 304A(b) of the Penal Code 1871."
#ASSERT (`charge under s 304A(a)` `A drives negligently and kills Z`)'s refusal EQUALS "A charge under section 304A(a) would assert that the facts fulfil every legal condition of causing death by rash act (CPC s 123(5)). On the facts given they do not: by doing a rash act."

`A drops a brick from a block knowing it may kill` MEANS `Rash Act Facts` WITH
    particulars                                                     IS `the particulars`
    victim                                                          IS ""
    `victim described as`                                           IS ""
    `the manner`                                                    IS "by throwing a brick from the 20th storey of Block 1 onto a walkway"
    `does the act rashly`                                           IS FALSE
    `does the act negligently`                                      IS FALSE
    `so as to endanger human life or the personal safety of others` IS TRUE
    `knowing or believing that such act is likely to cause death`   IS TRUE
    `causes hurt to any person`                                     IS FALSE
    `causes grievous hurt to any person`                            IS FALSE
    `causes the death of any person`                                IS FALSE
    `not amounting to culpable homicide`                            IS FALSE
#ASSERT `offence under s 335B` `A drops a brick from a block knowing it may kill`

§§ `Wrongful restraint and confinement - ss 339-348`

-- s 339 illus: A obstructs a path along which Z has a right to pass, A not
-- believing in good faith that he has a right to stop the path. Z is thereby
-- prevented from passing. A wrongfully restrains Z.
`s 339 illus` MEANS `Restraint Facts` WITH
    particulars                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                            IS `the particulars`
    victim                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                 IS "Z"
    `victim described as`                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                  IS ""
    `the manner`                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                           IS ""
    `voluntarily obstructs that person`                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    IS TRUE
    `so as to prevent that person from proceeding in any direction`                                                                                                                                                                                                        IS TRUE
    `in which that person has a right to proceed`                                                                                                                                                                                                                          IS TRUE
    `the obstruction is of a private way over land or water which he in good faith believes himself to have a lawful right to obstruct`                                                                                                                                    IS FALSE
    `in such a manner as to prevent that person from proceeding beyond certain circumscribing limits`                                                                                                                                                                      IS FALSE
    `knowing that a writ for the liberation of that person has been duly issued`                                                                                                                                                                                           IS FALSE
    `in such a manner as to indicate an intention that the confinement may not be known to any person interested or to any public servant, or that its place may not be known or discovered`                                                                               IS FALSE
    `for the purpose of extorting from the person confined, or from any person interested in him, any property or valuable security`                                                                                                                                       IS FALSE
    `for the purpose of constraining the person confined, or any person interested in him, to do anything illegal or to give any information which may facilitate the commission of an offence`                                                                            IS FALSE
    `for the purpose of extorting from the person confined, or from any person interested in him, any confession or any information which may lead to the detection of an offence or misconduct`                                                                           IS FALSE
    `for the purpose of constraining the person confined, or any person interested in him, to restore any property or valuable security, or to satisfy any claim or demand, or to give information which may lead to the restoration of any property or valuable security` IS FALSE
-- s 339 illus
#ASSERT `wrongfully restrains` `s 339 illus`
#ASSERT `offence under s 341` `s 339 illus`
#ASSERT NOT (`wrongfully confines` `s 339 illus`)
#ASSERT (`charge under s 341` `s 339 illus`)'s text EQUALS "You, A, are charged that you, on or about the 1st day of January 2026, at Orchard Road, Singapore, did wrongfully restrain one Z, and you have thereby committed an offence punishable under section 341 of the Penal Code 1871."

-- s 339 Exception: the same obstruction of a private way which A believes in
-- good faith he has a lawful right to obstruct is not an offence.
`s 339 Exception` MEANS `Restraint Facts` WITH
    particulars                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                            IS `the particulars`
    victim                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                 IS "Z"
    `victim described as`                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                  IS ""
    `the manner`                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                           IS ""
    `voluntarily obstructs that person`                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    IS TRUE
    `so as to prevent that person from proceeding in any direction`                                                                                                                                                                                                        IS TRUE
    `in which that person has a right to proceed`                                                                                                                                                                                                                          IS TRUE
    `the obstruction is of a private way over land or water which he in good faith believes himself to have a lawful right to obstruct`                                                                                                                                    IS TRUE
    `in such a manner as to prevent that person from proceeding beyond certain circumscribing limits`                                                                                                                                                                      IS FALSE
    `knowing that a writ for the liberation of that person has been duly issued`                                                                                                                                                                                           IS FALSE
    `in such a manner as to indicate an intention that the confinement may not be known to any person interested or to any public servant, or that its place may not be known or discovered`                                                                               IS FALSE
    `for the purpose of extorting from the person confined, or from any person interested in him, any property or valuable security`                                                                                                                                       IS FALSE
    `for the purpose of constraining the person confined, or any person interested in him, to do anything illegal or to give any information which may facilitate the commission of an offence`                                                                            IS FALSE
    `for the purpose of extorting from the person confined, or from any person interested in him, any confession or any information which may lead to the detection of an offence or misconduct`                                                                           IS FALSE
    `for the purpose of constraining the person confined, or any person interested in him, to restore any property or valuable security, or to satisfy any claim or demand, or to give information which may lead to the restoration of any property or valuable security` IS FALSE
-- s 339 Exception
#ASSERT NOT (`wrongfully restrains` `s 339 Exception`)

-- s 340 illus (a): A causes Z to go within a walled space, and locks Z in.
-- illus (b): A places men with firearms at the outlets of a building and
-- tells Z they will fire if Z attempts to leave. A wrongfully confines Z.
`s 340 illus (a)` MEANS `Restraint Facts` WITH
    particulars                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                            IS `the particulars`
    victim                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                 IS "Z"
    `victim described as`                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                  IS ""
    `the manner`                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                           IS "by locking the said Z in a walled compound"
    `voluntarily obstructs that person`                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    IS TRUE
    `so as to prevent that person from proceeding in any direction`                                                                                                                                                                                                        IS TRUE
    `in which that person has a right to proceed`                                                                                                                                                                                                                          IS TRUE
    `the obstruction is of a private way over land or water which he in good faith believes himself to have a lawful right to obstruct`                                                                                                                                    IS FALSE
    `in such a manner as to prevent that person from proceeding beyond certain circumscribing limits`                                                                                                                                                                      IS TRUE
    `knowing that a writ for the liberation of that person has been duly issued`                                                                                                                                                                                           IS FALSE
    `in such a manner as to indicate an intention that the confinement may not be known to any person interested or to any public servant, or that its place may not be known or discovered`                                                                               IS FALSE
    `for the purpose of extorting from the person confined, or from any person interested in him, any property or valuable security`                                                                                                                                       IS FALSE
    `for the purpose of constraining the person confined, or any person interested in him, to do anything illegal or to give any information which may facilitate the commission of an offence`                                                                            IS FALSE
    `for the purpose of extorting from the person confined, or from any person interested in him, any confession or any information which may lead to the detection of an offence or misconduct`                                                                           IS FALSE
    `for the purpose of constraining the person confined, or any person interested in him, to restore any property or valuable security, or to satisfy any claim or demand, or to give information which may lead to the restoration of any property or valuable security` IS FALSE
-- s 340 illus (a)
#ASSERT `wrongfully confines` `s 340 illus (a)`
#ASSERT `offence under s 342` `s 340 illus (a)`
#ASSERT (`charge under s 342` `s 340 illus (a)`)'s text EQUALS "You, A, are charged that you, on or about the 1st day of January 2026, at Orchard Road, Singapore, did wrongfully confine one Z, to wit, by locking the said Z in a walled compound, and you have thereby committed an offence punishable under section 342 of the Penal Code 1871."
-- s 340 illus (b) is illus (a) on the same atoms: the obstruction by threat of
-- firearms is `voluntarily obstructs that person` (its @desc says so).
#ASSERT `wrongfully confines` `s 340 illus (a)`

-- s 347: confined for ransom.
`A confines Z for ransom` MEANS `Restraint Facts` WITH
    particulars                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                            IS `the particulars`
    victim                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                 IS "Z"
    `victim described as`                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                  IS ""
    `the manner`                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                           IS "by keeping the said Z in a locked room until his family paid $50,000"
    `voluntarily obstructs that person`                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    IS TRUE
    `so as to prevent that person from proceeding in any direction`                                                                                                                                                                                                        IS TRUE
    `in which that person has a right to proceed`                                                                                                                                                                                                                          IS TRUE
    `the obstruction is of a private way over land or water which he in good faith believes himself to have a lawful right to obstruct`                                                                                                                                    IS FALSE
    `in such a manner as to prevent that person from proceeding beyond certain circumscribing limits`                                                                                                                                                                      IS TRUE
    `knowing that a writ for the liberation of that person has been duly issued`                                                                                                                                                                                           IS FALSE
    `in such a manner as to indicate an intention that the confinement may not be known to any person interested or to any public servant, or that its place may not be known or discovered`                                                                               IS FALSE
    `for the purpose of extorting from the person confined, or from any person interested in him, any property or valuable security`                                                                                                                                       IS TRUE
    `for the purpose of constraining the person confined, or any person interested in him, to do anything illegal or to give any information which may facilitate the commission of an offence`                                                                            IS FALSE
    `for the purpose of extorting from the person confined, or from any person interested in him, any confession or any information which may lead to the detection of an offence or misconduct`                                                                           IS FALSE
    `for the purpose of constraining the person confined, or any person interested in him, to restore any property or valuable security, or to satisfy any claim or demand, or to give information which may lead to the restoration of any property or valuable security` IS FALSE
#ASSERT `offence under s 347` `A confines Z for ransom`
#ASSERT NOT (`offence under s 348` `A confines Z for ransom`)

§§ `Criminal force and assault - ss 349-358`

-- s 350 illus (a): A unfastens the moorings of Z's boat, which drifts. A has
-- intentionally used force to Z (by disposing substances); if without Z's
-- consent and intending injury, fear or annoyance, criminal force.
`s 350 illus (a)` MEANS `Criminal Force Facts` WITH
    particulars                                                                                                                                                                                                  IS `the particulars`
    victim                                                                                                                                                                                                       IS "Z"
    `victim described as`                                                                                                                                                                                        IS ""
    `the manner`                                                                                                                                                                                                 IS ""
    `causes motion, change of motion, or cessation of motion to that other`                                                                                                                                      IS TRUE
    `causes to any substance such motion as brings that substance into contact with that other's body, or with anything he is wearing or carrying, or so situated that the contact affects his sense of feeling` IS FALSE
    `by his own bodily power`                                                                                                                                                                                    IS FALSE
    `by disposing any substance so that the motion takes place without any further act`                                                                                                                          IS TRUE
    `by inducing any animal to move, to change its motion, or to cease to move`                                                                                                                                  IS FALSE
    `intentionally uses force`                                                                                                                                                                                   IS TRUE
    `without that person's consent`                                                                                                                                                                              IS TRUE
    `in order to cause the committing of any offence`                                                                                                                                                            IS FALSE
    `intending by the use of such force illegally to cause injury, fear or annoyance to that person`                                                                                                             IS TRUE
    `knowing it to be likely that by the use of such force he will illegally cause injury, fear or annoyance to that person`                                                                                     IS FALSE
    `makes any gesture or any preparation`                                                                                                                                                                       IS FALSE
    `intending or knowing it to be likely that it will cause any person present to apprehend that he is about to use criminal force to that person`                                                              IS FALSE
    `on grave and sudden provocation given by that person`                                                                                                                                                       IS FALSE
    `the provocation is not sought or voluntarily provoked by the offender as an excuse for the offence`                                                                                                         IS FALSE
    `the offender does not know or have reason to believe that the provocation is given by anything done in obedience to the law or by a public servant in the lawful exercise of his powers`                    IS FALSE
    `the provocation is not given by anything done in the lawful exercise of the right of private defence`                                                                                                       IS FALSE
    `that person is a public servant`                                                                                                                                                                            IS FALSE
    `in the execution of his duty as such public servant`                                                                                                                                                        IS FALSE
    `with intent to prevent or deter that person from discharging his duty as such public servant`                                                                                                               IS FALSE
    `in consequence of anything done or attempted to be done by such person in the lawful discharge of his duty as such public servant`                                                                          IS FALSE
    `intending to outrage the modesty of that person`                                                                                                                                                            IS FALSE
    `knowing it to be likely that he will thereby outrage the modesty of that person`                                                                                                                            IS FALSE
    `that person is below 14 years of age`                                                                                                                                                                       IS FALSE
    `in order to commit or to facilitate the commission of an offence against that person under section 354`                                                                                                     IS FALSE
    `voluntarily causes or attempts to cause to that person death`                                                                                                                                               IS FALSE
    `voluntarily causes or attempts to cause to that person hurt`                                                                                                                                                IS FALSE
    `voluntarily causes or attempts to cause to that person wrongful restraint`                                                                                                                                  IS FALSE
    `voluntarily causes or attempts to cause to that person fear of instant death, instant hurt or instant wrongful restraint`                                                                                   IS FALSE
    `in a lift in any building`                                                                                                                                                                                  IS FALSE
    `intending thereby to dishonour that person`                                                                                                                                                                 IS FALSE
    `in committing or attempting to commit theft of any property which that person is then wearing or carrying`                                                                                                  IS FALSE
    `in attempting wrongfully to confine that person`                                                                                                                                                            IS FALSE
-- s 350 illus (a)
#ASSERT `uses force` `s 350 illus (a)`
#ASSERT `uses criminal force` `s 350 illus (a)`

