§§ `Offences affecting life - ss 299-318`

-- s 299 illus (a): A lays sticks and turf over a pit, intending death or
-- knowing death likely. Z treads on it, falls in and is killed. Culpable
-- homicide.
`s 299 illus (a)` MEANS `Homicide Facts` WITH
    particulars                                                                                                                                                                                             IS `the particulars`
    victim                                                                                                                                                                                                  IS "Z"
    `victim described as`                                                                                                                                                                                   IS ""
    `the manner`                                                                                                                                                                                            IS ""
    `causes death by doing an act`                                                                                                                                                                          IS TRUE
    `with the intention of causing death`                                                                                                                                                                   IS FALSE
    `with the intention of causing such bodily injury as is likely to cause death`                                                                                                                          IS FALSE
    `with the knowledge that he is likely by such act to cause death`                                                                                                                                       IS TRUE
    `with the intention of causing such bodily injury as the offender knows to be likely to cause the death of the person to whom the harm is caused`                                                       IS FALSE
    `with the intention of causing bodily injury to any person`                                                                                                                                             IS FALSE
    `the bodily injury intended to be inflicted is sufficient in the ordinary course of nature to cause death`                                                                                              IS FALSE
    `knows that the act is so imminently dangerous that it must in all probability cause death, or such bodily injury as is likely to cause death`                                                          IS FALSE
    `commits such act without any excuse for incurring the risk of causing death or such injury`                                                                                                            IS FALSE
    `whilst deprived of the power of self-control by grave and sudden provocation`                                                                                                                          IS FALSE
    `causes the death of the person who gave the provocation, or of any other person by mistake or accident`                                                                                                IS FALSE
    `the provocation is not sought or voluntarily provoked by the offender as an excuse for killing or doing harm to any person`                                                                            IS FALSE
    `the offender did not know and had no reason to believe that the provocation was given by anything done in obedience to the law, or by a public servant in the lawful exercise of his powers`           IS FALSE
    `the provocation is not given by anything done in the lawful exercise of the right of private defence`                                                                                                  IS FALSE
    `in the exercise of the right of private defence of person or property, exceeds the power given to him by law`                                                                                          IS FALSE
    `causes the death of the person against whom he is exercising such right of defence`                                                                                                                    IS FALSE
    `without premeditation formed prior to the circumstances which gave rise to the act of private defence`                                                                                                 IS FALSE
    `without any intention of doing more harm than is necessary for the purpose of such defence`                                                                                                            IS FALSE
    `being a public servant, or aiding a public servant acting for the advancement of public justice, exceeds the powers given to him by law`                                                               IS FALSE
    `causes death by doing an act which he, in good faith, believes to be lawful and necessary for the due discharge of his duty as such public servant`                                                    IS FALSE
    `without ill will towards the person whose death is caused`                                                                                                                                             IS FALSE
    `without premeditation formed prior to the circumstances constituting the sudden fight`                                                                                                                 IS FALSE
    `in a sudden fight`                                                                                                                                                                                     IS FALSE
    `in the heat of passion upon a sudden quarrel`                                                                                                                                                          IS FALSE
    `without the offender having taken undue advantage or acted in a cruel or unusual manner`                                                                                                               IS FALSE
    `the offender did not know and had no reason to believe that the person whose death was caused was acting in obedience to the law, or was a public servant acting in the lawful exercise of his powers` IS FALSE
    `the person whose death is caused is above 18 years of age`                                                                                                                                             IS FALSE
    `suffers death or takes the risk of death with his own consent`                                                                                                                                         IS FALSE
    `the offender being a woman voluntarily causes the death of her child`                                                                                                                                  IS FALSE
    `the child is below 12 months of age`                                                                                                                                                                   IS FALSE
    `the balance of her mind was disturbed by reason of her not having fully recovered from the effect of giving birth to the child or by reason of the effect of lactation`                                IS FALSE
    `suffering from such abnormality of mind as substantially impaired his capacity to know the nature of the acts or omissions`                                                                            IS FALSE
    `substantially impaired capacity to know that the acts or omissions are wrong by the ordinary standards of reasonable and honest persons`                                                               IS FALSE
    `substantially impaired capacity to know that the acts or omissions are wrong as contrary to law`                                                                                                       IS FALSE
    `suffering from such abnormality of mind as substantially impaired his power to control his acts or omissions`                                                                                          IS FALSE
    `under such circumstances that if he by that act caused death he would be guilty of murder`                                                                                                             IS FALSE
    `under such circumstances that if he by that act caused death he would be guilty of culpable homicide not amounting to murder`                                                                          IS FALSE
    `hurt is caused to any person by such act`                                                                                                                                                              IS FALSE
    `under sentence of imprisonment for life`                                                                                                                                                               IS FALSE
-- s 299 illus (a)
#ASSERT `commits culpable homicide` `s 299 illus (a)`

